    {
      "id": "q5n32sa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "17.4 Exam Strategy & Preparation Tips"
    },
    {
      "id": "qo3onpe",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>KARNATAKA SI EXAM — STRATEGY GUIDE</strong></p><p><strong>PAPER 1 — GENERAL KNOWLEDGE &amp; CURRENT AFFAIRS:</strong></p><p>  1. Karnataka-specific topics carry 40–50% weight in Paper 1. Master this guide first.</p><p>  2. Read The Hindu / Deccan Herald daily for Karnataka current affairs — 3 months before exam.</p><p>  3. Memorise all 31 districts: HQ, division, bordering states, known for. Use a blank map to practice.</p><p>  4. Dynasties in order: Kadambas → Chalukyas → Rashtrakutas → W. Chalukyas → Hoysalas → Vijayanagara. Never mix capitals.</p><p>  5. Agriculture ranks: Coffee (1st), Arecanut (1st), Silk (2nd), Ragi (1st), Sunflower (1st). Memorise these.</p><p><strong>PAPER 2 — BNS / BNSS / BSA &amp; KARNATAKA POLICE ACT:</strong></p><p>  6. Buy a bare act copy of BNS 2023 and read Section 1–50 + 100–113 carefully — new concepts.</p><p>  7. Compare BNS with IPC: Murder: 302 → 101; Rape: 375 → 63; Cheating: 420 → 318. Key changes.</p><p>  8. BNSS: Zero FIR (Sec 173), Forensic mandatory (Sec 176), 60-day remand for serious cases — tested frequently.</p><p>  9. Karnataka Police Act 1963: Section 20 (duties), 27 (disperse), 34 (prohibit), 41 (public duty to inform) — essential.</p><p>  10. Constitution: Art. 19 (6 freedoms), 21 (life &amp; liberty), 22 (arrest), 32 (remedies) — must know word for word.</p><p><strong>PAPER 3 — ENGLISH:</strong></p><p>  11. Practise spotting grammatical errors daily — subject-verb agreement, tense, prepositions.</p><p>  12. Learn police/legal vocabulary: subpoena, cognizable, bailable, FIR, chargesheet, cognizance, remand.</p><p>  13. Reading comprehension: read the questions BEFORE the passage to save time.</p><p><strong>GENERAL TIPS:</strong></p><p>  14. Negative marking: -0.25 per wrong answer in most Karnataka police exams — skip doubtful questions.</p><p>  15. Previous year papers (2018–2024 KPSC / Karnataka Police Recruitment): solve minimum 5 full sets.</p><p>  16. Physical test: practice 100m sprint, long jump. Medical fitness — eyesight test is strict (6/6 for SI).</p><p>  17. Character &amp; background verification: maintain clean record; any criminal case can disqualify.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
